A procedure written with mixed-case keywords (`:Declare`, `:EndIf`,
`:Return`) among correct ones. Keywords are case-sensitive, so each
miscased token is keyword_uppercase (error) with the canonical spelling;
correctly cased keywords and keyword names used as plain words
(`Return` inside a string) do not flag (diag.keyword_uppercase).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CheckStock;
	:PARAMETERS nOnHand;
	:Declare sMessage;
	sMessage := "Return to supplier";
	:IF nOnHand > 0;
		sMessage := "In stock";
	:EndIf;
	:Return sMessage;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CheckStock;
	:PARAMETERS nOnHand;
	:DECLARE sMessage;
	sMessage := "Return to supplier";
	:IF nOnHand > 0;
		sMessage := "In stock";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sMessage;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:2-3:10 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':DECLARE'
7:2-7:8 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':ENDIF'
8:2-8:9 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':RETURN'
